{
  "evidence": "TEXT_E: “Get Brexit done… UK makes its own laws, controls… borders and trade; Strengthen the Union”; Crime/justice: 20,000 more police, tougher sentencing, more stop-and-search, extra prison places; Immigration: Australian-style points system, reduce low‑skilled migration, 5‑year wait for most benefits, higher NHS surcharge; Defence: exceed NATO 2%, Trident, Space Command, extensive veterans’ support; Constitution: voter ID, keep First Past the Post, equalised constituencies; Economy/tax: no rises in main taxes, business support, tougher anti‑avoidance; NHS record funding and social care pledges; Environment: Net Zero 2050, plastics crackdown, tree planting.\nTEXT_D: Stop Brexit and embrace EU freedom of movement; Policing/justice: presumption against short prison sentences, focus on rehabilitation; Rights/equality: Human Rights Act/ECHR defence, gender recognition reforms, X‑gender passports, pay‑gap reporting; Welfare: scrap sanctions, right to food, raise housing support, abolish bedroom tax; Immigration/asylum: end hostile environment, right to work for asylum seekers, resettlement commitments; Democracy: proportional representation, Lords reform, citizens’ assemblies, federal UK/devolution; Strong climate targets (Net Zero 2045, fracking ban); NHS/social care funded by 1p Income Tax rise, mental health parity.",
  "reasoning": "Because Authority and Loyalty are the electorate’s top priorities, TEXT_E’s emphasis on sovereignty, border control, policing and tougher sentencing, defence/veterans, and maintaining traditional institutions aligns strongly, while also offering Proportionality (tax restraint/benefit rules) and some Care/Sanctity (NHS and environmental measures). TEXT_D prioritizes Equality and Care (expanded welfare and rights, immigration openness, rehabilitative justice, devolution/PR) with less focus on Authority/Loyalty, making it a weaker match to the profile.",
  "confidence": "high",
  "winner": "TEXT_E"
}
